{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Variables in PHP", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 3, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 2, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "You can make use of these words to talk about PHP.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Understand information about web applications, their principles and basic concepts in a range of work contexts.   Describe applications for an operating system for personal computers in a range of work contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.\t Exchanges simple information on web applications, and applications for operating systems for personal computers.", "type": "secondary_1"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le02ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "must ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something that is necessary ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In addition, it's a must that all variables start with the $ sign. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le02ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "scope", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the range or extent of a variable", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Scopes are the parts of scripts, in which a variable is used or referenced.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le02ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "give a hand ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to help someone", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Mary, could you give me a hand, please?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le02ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "declare ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to announce; in programming, it refers to write codes", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In this case, PHP doesn't have a command which can declare a variable. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le02ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "case-sensitive ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "related to the use of capital letters", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Remember that variables are case-sensitive, too.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le02ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Review the rules of PHP variables. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Design a sample of a PHP variable. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Give value to each informational data you have. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Select different PHP scopes for the same sample. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present to your partners or instructor.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I design a sample of a PHP variable. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I give value and scope to variable information. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I explain what can and cannot be included in the PHP variable that I created. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use visual aids to present my sample.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Passive of Modal Verbs: Can", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "We use the <b>passive voice</b> when we want to emphasize in the action and not in the person who does it. </br>Passive voice can be used anytime; we are going to focus on can and how to use it in negative sentences this time.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<strong>Can</strong>, in negative sentences, is used to refer to forbidden situations or facts that are not possible.</br></br>  Look at the following structure: <center> </br> Subject + <b>can't/cannot + be + verb in past participle </b> + complement</br></br> </center> Examples: </br><i> The cd room <b>can't be considered </b> as something modern anymore.  </br> Variables <b>can't be created just </b>by numbers. </i>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The sign $ cannot be changed in the PHP variables.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The name of variables cannot be followed by numbers. ", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Declaring Variables in PHP", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "There are rules to follow if you want to declare a variable in PHP.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "To declare or create a variable in PHP, consider the following rules:</br> <br> - Start with the sign $; then, write the name of the variable.</br> - The name must start with a letter or underscore character, it can't start with a number.</br> - It can make use of the alpha-numeric characters and underscores.</br> - They are case-sensitive.</br> <br> Examples:</br> <br>$txt</br> $y</br> $Y: this one is different from $y because it is case-sensitive.</br> $total_volume</br></br>  ", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "I can say what a variable in PHP is.   ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can present the rules of PHP variables.   ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "What are the purposes of variables? ", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "Are variables created the same way in different programming lang